        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-693",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "`scan_huggingface_model` applies the identical defective extension allowlist, omitting `_numpy_file_extensions`. At scanner.py:585 the filter is `if file_ext not in _zip_file_extensions and file_ext not in _pickle_file_extensions and file_ext not in _pytorch_file_extensions: continue`, applied to each `rfilename` from the HuggingFace `/api/models/{repo_id}` siblings listing. Any `.npy` file published in a HuggingFace model repo is therefore never downloaded and never scanned, even though the very next lines (588-590) would have dispatched it correctly via `scan_bytes(data, url, file_ext)` \u2192 `scan_numpy`. This is the exact scenario picklescan exists to defend (`picklescan -hf <model>` as a pre-download gate), so the gap directly defeats the tool's stated purpose for one file format it otherwise fully supports.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived from source. scanner.py:585-586 gates every HuggingFace sibling `rfilename` on an allowlist of only `_zip_file_extensions`, `_pickle_file_extensions` and `_pytorch_file_extensions`; `_numpy_file_extensions` (= {\".npy\"}, defined line 217) is omitted, so any `.npy` in a model repo hits `continue` at 586 and is never downloaded (588-589) nor scanned (590), and is not even counted in `scanned_files` \u2014 the CLI prints a clean summary. The capability being bypassed demonstrably exists: scan_bytes:561-562 dispatches `.npy` to scan_numpy, and scan_numpy:482-515 scans the embedded pickle when `dtype.hasobject`. The repo's own test corpus proves the payload class is real and detectable by other entry points: tests/init_data_files.py:911 builds a weaponized `data2/dns_exfiltration.npy` and tests/test_scanner.py:181 asserts scan_file_path flags it. README.md:41 advertises `.npy` support, so this is a gap rather than a documented exclusion; `.npz` is covered only incidentally via `_zip_file_extensions`. Reachability is confirmed, not assumed: cli.py:36-40 and 67-68 wire `-hf/--huggingface` straight into scan_huggingface_model, and a graph query shows the line-585 condition and the line-590 `scan_bytes` call with reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1. The identical defect recurs at 603-608 in scan_directory_path. Severity MEDIUM, not HIGH: it is a total false negative in the tool's stated pre-download gate for one supported format, but downstream RCE additionally needs the victim to use `np.load(..., allow_pickle=True)` (numpy defaults to False since 1.16.3). exploit_search returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\" for picklescan 1.0.0 (setup.cfg:3), so no published-module evidence is claimed in either direction."
          },
